WEBVTT

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:05.360
Tomorrow's finally the day 
of our quest practical!

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.780
Uh-huh! I can't wait!

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:10.880
Adventuring is all about quests!

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.990
A Hero's someone who does lots of quests 
and helps all kinds of people, too!

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:17.620
This is just a part of our lessons,

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.600
so I'm sure we'll only be 
given very basic quests.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.550
What kind of quest do you want
 to take on, Yusha-san?

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:26.440
Well, when you think of Heroes,

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:28.750
you think of dragon-slaying!

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:34.040
Sure, and at our current level,
 we'd all be wiped out within five seconds.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.890
I told you, they'll just be basic quests.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.770
Then what kind of quest would you all like?

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.520
Well...

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.360
Oh! A quest to eat lots of yummy things!

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:49.530
A quest from someone who wants 
us to get some rare Cartado!

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:52.300
There's no quest like that.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.780
Then what kind of quest 
would you like, Sei-chan?

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:57.380
Huh? Well...

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:00.160
Oh!

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:03.290
Something like a quest to stop 
a rampaging horned gorilla!

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:06.420
Uh, you mean a horned gorilla slaying?

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:09.660
No, not to slay one.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:12.670
A quest to persuade and soothe one.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:15.390
Like you do with a person 
holding up a building?

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:18.940
When you tell them,
"You're making your mother cry"?

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:19.560
Yeah.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:24.800
Then the horned gorilla would return 
to his home thanks to our persuasion,

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.830
and the horned gorilla I persuaded

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:29.270
would secretly be a candidate 
for the horned gorilla king,

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:32.190
caught up in a battle for 
power between factions.

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:35.480
But then I'd go back with 
the contender for the throne

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:38.580
and aid him in his battle to fight 
corruption in the horned gorilla world.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:42.700
But then his long-lost brother, the former 
king's illegitimate son, would appear

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:46.700
and claim he was the rightful heir to 
the throne, and take over the kingdom!

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:48.350
After being driven out of the kingdom,

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:51.110
we'd go searching throughout their 
hidden land of Horned Gonglia

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:54.460
for the legendary, sacred sword Exgorilla,

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.380
but along the way,
 we'd be caught in a twister.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:59.210
Our cart would be launched into
the land of Goth in another world,

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:00.970
where we'd meet the 
Horned Gorilla Witch of the West...

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.780
Endro!

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:35.480
Roll 3

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:38.990
Adventurer's Guild

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:45.550
It's awesome that we get to accept 
a quest from a real guild!

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:47.370
I wonder what kind of quest it'll be.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:50.680
Still, it's just a practical quest,
 so I'm sure it's just,

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:53.630
"Go to the next town over 
and buy some things for me,"

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:57.400
or "Go deliver this message to the next 
town over," or something like that.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:00.880
So, the quest we have for you is,

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:05.260
"Go obtain the whisker of a flying ocean 
sunfish from the shores of Star Coral."

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:06.640
Okay!

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:12.520
Your quest is, "Go obtain the fruit
 of a wind piper from Black Elm Forest."

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:13.650
Right!

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:16.020
They sound pretty good to me!

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:17.730
Maybe we can get our hopes up.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:20.050
There's no horned gorilla quest.

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:21.190
I know!

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:23.650
Now us, please!

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:28.530
A party of just women? That's unusual.

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:33.920
You're a Priest, you're a Warrior, 
and you're a Mage, I see.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:35.600
And you are?

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:37.420
A Hero!

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.550
Ah, right. There <i>are</i> some people like that.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:42.050
D'oh!

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:43.450
Don't worry!

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:46.310
Even if you're not a Hero,
 you're still Yusha!

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.310
Smug

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.310
Either way, Yu shine!

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:51.030
That wasn't a very good pun.

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:53.690
So that's when you give it to me straight...

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:56.440
Okay, I'll tell you your quest now.

00:04:57.110 --> 00:04:58.780
Your quest is...

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:01.190
"Find a cat."

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.330
Oh, you've found him?

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:12.700
Good job.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:14.230
Here's your reward.

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:17.250
There's still more to the practical,

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:19.340
so work hard again tomorrow.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:27.470
Is looking for cats really 
something adventurers do?

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:32.540
"Quest" means searching for something, 
so they're not wrong in that respect.

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:36.190
Now that you mention it, adventurers 
are always out looking for something.

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:39.420
Searching for treasures,
 searching for captured princesses,

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:41.860
searching for legendary monsters...

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:46.620
Adventurers aren't so much professional 
combatants as professional seekers, I guess.

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:47.560
Yeah.

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:52.630
So the next time we lose our room keys, 
we can ask adventurers to find them!

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:55.240
Except we're those adventurers.

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:57.940
What?! Then we'd have to find them ourselves?

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:02.660
Then once we become adventurers,
 it won't be eating lots of yummy food,

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:05.390
but just a bunch of "Find this food" quests?

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:08.260
Yeah, that's much more likely.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:09.900
That's awful!

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:12.140
If I find something yummy, I want to eat it!

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:13.210
I get that!

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:16.770
When I find yummy bread in Seira-chan's 
bag, I can't help but eat it!

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:18.150
Yeah, exactly!

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:20.720
No, you don't! You two eat too much!

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:22.200
What?!

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:23.530
Oh, come on.

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:27.480
Even Mei wouldn't wear Cartado
 she just picked up off the ground.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:28.410
I wouldn't.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:30.410
What if it was a rare one?

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:33.040
I wouldn't.

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:34.160
What was that pause for?

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:36.410
I get it, Sei-chan.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:42.540
Even if we get a quest to find 
something delicious, I won't eat it.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:43.830
You're crying over this?

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:47.920
Adventurer's Guild

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:56.930
Your quest is, "Go obtain a fire lizard's 
egg from Red Ice Mountain."

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:58.190
All right!

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:04.940
Your quest is, "Go obtain the oil of a 
mica frog from the Pond of Poison Mist."

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:06.440
Understood!

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:09.930
So, I wonder what quest we'll get today.

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:14.070
I don't care, as long as it's not a quest
 to find something delicious.

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:17.940
I can h-hold myself back!

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:21.550
Now us, please!

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:24.260
Oh, it's you four.

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:25.460
Yeah!

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:29.130
All right, I hope you get 
an interesting quest.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:30.090
Let's see...

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:33.100
Your quest is...

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:34.910
"Find a cat."

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:37.220
What?!

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:40.880
Um, could you give us a different one?

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:44.520
Nope. You don't get to choose 
your quests during the practical.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.730
We're supposed to assign them at random.

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:49.740
But that's twice in a row
 we've had to find a cat.

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:52.030
If you don't like it, you can drop out.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:55.160
We don't want to drop out.

00:07:56.470 --> 00:07:57.160
I know!

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:59.720
Let's take on an additional quest!

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:01.660
We took care of finding a cat yesterday,

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.170
so we can finish it up quickly!

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:04.880
I get it!

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.860
Huh? Are you sure?

00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:15.120
It's kind of incredible that we pulled 
"Find a cat" five times in a row.

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:16.740
Seriously.

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:20.100
I wonder why we didn't stop 
after the third one.

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:22.560
Uh-huh, that's just how it goes.

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:24.940
At this point, we just have to do it!

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:32.570
Oh! You found all five!

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:34.200
Good job.

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:35.290
Here's your reward.

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:37.680
Work hard again tomorrow!

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:44.460
Today was tough.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:49.700
But you know, I think we've gotten 
the hang of finding cats now!

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:50.400
Yeah!

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:53.940
If we keep this up, we could 
probably find cats professionally!

00:08:53.940 --> 00:08:55.800
Oh! That might be nice!

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:58.760
We'd know right away when 
cute kitties are in the area!

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:00.460
Hey, hey, hey!

00:09:00.460 --> 00:09:03.350
We're still the Hero's Party,
 one way or another.

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:07.900
Once the Demon Lord revives, how can we 
fight him if we're professional cat finders?

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:10.050
Um, well...

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:15.110
Demon Lord

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:15.110
Me

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:15.430
Bow before my power!

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:20.450
Go now, the cutest kitties 
I could find and collect!

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:26.500
Oh, what cute kitties you are!

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:27.740
How's that, Demon Lord?!

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:30.570
If you continue to do evil,
 I'm taking all these kitties home!

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:31.340
What?

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:32.940
Don't do that!

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:35.840
I can't live without these kitties anymore!

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:41.470
I'll forgive you.

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:41.470
Me

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:38.680
Then you won't do evil anymore, will you?!

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:41.470
I won't do anything evil anymore!

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:43.520
And all live happily ever after!

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:45.560
Like that!

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:48.670
That certainly sounds peaceful.

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:49.950
That'd be great!

00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:50.730
Right?

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:55.020
Then I'll need to gather up all 
the Cartado dealing with cats.

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:56.490
Those exist?

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:59.990
Adventurer's Guild

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:01.990
Hello!

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:04.060
Oh, it's you four.

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:07.570
So, what type of cat are we looking for today?

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:09.500
Calico? Spotted? Bring it on!

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:12.190
We're used to it after six times.

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:16.140
I did some research yesterday and 
found a Cartado with a catnip spell!

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:17.630
There really was one?

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:25.020
Your quest is, "Go obtain moonlight 
moss from Silver Bone Cave."

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:29.400
Uh... That's a long name for a cat.

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:30.750
It's not a cat!

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:36.360
Your quest is, "Go obtain moonlight 
moss from Silver Bone Cave."

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:38.200
You mean...

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:39.740
Is it really...

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.240
Could it be...

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:43.240
We're not looking for a cat?

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:45.250
Exactly.

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:49.120
H-Hooray!

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:52.260
The Silver Bone Cave, huh?

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:53.760
Where was that again?

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:57.880
If I recall, it's about two hours south of here.

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:00.260
Oh, that's pretty far.

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:02.570
We'll need to equip ourselves first.

00:11:02.570 --> 00:11:04.830
Oh, should I bring our barbecue set?

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:07.100
What are you talking about?

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:09.270
We're not going there to have fun.

00:11:15.220 --> 00:11:16.280
What's the matter?

00:11:18.330 --> 00:11:20.800
Michael's gone.

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:22.160
Michael?

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:25.790
My cat. He's all white, with 
black on just the tip of his tail.

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:26.640
Huh?

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:29.860
He's been with me since the day I was born,

00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:32.190
but when I woke up this 
morning, he was gone.

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:34.620
I don't know where he is...

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:41.800
All right! We'll go find him for you!

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:43.430
What? Really?

00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:44.680
What? Really?

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:47.810
Is that okay?

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:51.590
Don't worry.

00:11:51.590 --> 00:11:54.060
We're professional cat finders.

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:56.690
We found five just yesterday!

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:59.950
I have my catnip Cartado, too.

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:01.450
Everyone...

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:05.080
We'll find Michael-chan for you,
 so don't worry.

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:07.200
Thank you!

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:09.340
Leave it to us!

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:12.200
<i>ENDRO!</i>

00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:21.470
I'm sorry. We wound up 
looking for a cat anyway.

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:23.460
What are you saying?

00:12:23.460 --> 00:12:26.240
A Hero is someone who helps people in need.

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:27.350
That was for the best.

00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:29.730
Oh! You praised her for once!

00:12:29.730 --> 00:12:33.190
It's not as if I hate her.

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:35.030
I praise her when I think she's done good.

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:38.360
I-I love you too, Seira-chan!

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:40.580
I love you too, Sei-chan!

00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:41.850
Me, too!

00:12:41.850 --> 00:12:43.910
Why are you two jumping on the bandwagon?

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:45.370
I didn't want to lose to her.

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:46.370
Same!

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:49.870
More importantly, we need to find the cat.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.040
Come on, let's hurry up!

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:53.470
Right!

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:06.760
You think Michael-chan
 is really in a place like this?

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:11.390
The people in town said they saw one
 that matched his description in this area.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:14.550
Apparently, when a cat enters 
another's territory,

00:13:14.550 --> 00:13:17.440
they get chased around and driven 
farther and farther away.

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:20.570
At this point, he's more than lost.
He's on a journey.

00:13:21.520 --> 00:13:24.010
This monster's incredibly slow.

00:13:24.010 --> 00:13:25.230
This'll be easy!

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:26.240
All right.

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:37.020
Huh? We won.

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:38.500
We did it!

00:13:39.490 --> 00:13:41.000
A treasure chest!

00:13:42.390 --> 00:13:44.200
Oh, more grass.

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:45.380
It's a medicinal herb.

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:48.700
These aren't very yummy, either.

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:51.180
Because they're medicine, not food.

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:53.830
Oh. The sun's already setting.

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:56.640
You're right. Should we head 
back to town for the day?

00:13:58.590 --> 00:14:01.150
Since we're here, let's camp out!

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:09.520
Who would have thought we'd be 
camping out while looking for a cat?

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:10.600
Seriously.

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:13.780
But this feels more like adventuring!

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:15.990
It's making me excited!

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:17.940
Oh, my.

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:20.110
Well, shall we make dinner?

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:22.800
Yay! Food, food!

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:30.180
Huh?

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:34.780
You were in charge of our provisions, 
weren't you, Seira-chan?

00:14:34.780 --> 00:14:36.180
That's not right.

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:37.300
Oh, I get it!

00:14:37.300 --> 00:14:41.470
You're going out hunting now 
to bring us back some fresh meat!

00:14:41.470 --> 00:14:42.730
That's incredible!

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:43.190
Huh?!

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:45.430
N-N-N-No way, no way, no way, no way!

00:14:45.430 --> 00:14:47.670
It's already night, and I can't see very well!

00:14:47.670 --> 00:14:50.570
Besides, I'm not that good with a bow, either!

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:54.580
That reminds me. You always use a hammer,
 even though you're an elf.

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:55.890
Yes, that's right!

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:59.620
Huh? Then why did you bring
a bow instead of food?

00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:03.300
I just brought the wrong thing by mistake.

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:04.640
What?!

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:05.460
I'm sorry.

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:07.720
We have no food?

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:10.020
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:12.460
I'll go back right now and get food for us!

00:15:12.460 --> 00:15:14.380
Uh, I should make it by dawn...

00:15:14.380 --> 00:15:14.970
No way.

00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:16.960
I won't last that long.

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:20.440
The thought of having no food to eat 
is making me even more hungry.

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:22.420
Wait! Wait, Fai!

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:23.230
Oh, Mei!

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:26.230
You showed me an "Imperial Feast" 
Cartado the other day, right?

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:27.620
Do you have that with you?!

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:28.570
I do.

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:30.330
Use it right now!

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:31.440
I can't.

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:32.800
Huh?! Why not?

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:34.740
Did you forget to fill up your mana?

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:38.230
No, it's a legendary rare 
that's way beyond just rare,

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:40.090
so I want to preserve it unused.

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:41.120
What?!

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:44.480
I'm so... hungry...

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:46.860
I'm starving!

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:56.480
Can I take this off?

00:15:56.480 --> 00:16:00.500
Not until Yusha-san comes 
back from town with food.

00:16:01.080 --> 00:16:05.770
Um, could you please use 
your "Imperial Feast" for us?

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:09.760
I'd rather fall into the swirling 
miasma of a dark world,

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:11.380
turn the entire world against me,

00:16:11.380 --> 00:16:15.280
and start a bloody war that 
may never end than use it.

00:16:15.590 --> 00:16:17.490
Right...

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:24.130
Augh! Yusha, hurry back!

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:35.370
I'll never forget our food again.

00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:38.800
I don't remember anything from 
last night. Did something happen?

00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:41.120
Oh, I can see a tower!

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:43.790
That must be the tower 
the townsfolk mentioned.

00:16:44.820 --> 00:16:48.470
Michael-san has gotten himself 
lost in an incredible place.

00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:51.420
But isn't this something you'd 
see on a real adventure?

00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:52.480
Yeah.

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:55.140
All right, off to adventure!

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:56.340
Yeah!

00:16:56.340 --> 00:16:57.560
Hey, wait!

00:16:57.560 --> 00:16:58.910
You're getting too excited.

00:17:05.280 --> 00:17:07.200
Welcome, travelers.

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:08.920
This is Red Spider Tower.

00:17:13.060 --> 00:17:16.420
Um, have you seen a white cat?

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:18.810
One with black on just the tip of his tail?

00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:24.440
Yes, I saw a cat with such a pattern
 on the top floor of this tower.

00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:26.440
R-Really?

00:17:27.220 --> 00:17:28.960
Thank you very much.

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:35.220
Why do you think that guy was 
standing out here the whole time?

00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:37.200
That must be his job.

00:17:37.470 --> 00:17:40.200
Oh. Well, we should be grateful.

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:49.660
I see what looks like traps scattered about,

00:17:49.660 --> 00:17:51.630
and it sounds like there are monsters inside.

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:55.760
It's probably going to be difficult 
to reach the top floor.

00:17:56.040 --> 00:18:01.700
But that regular-looking guy at the entrance 
said he'd been to the top floor,

00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:03.490
so maybe it's easier than we think.

00:18:03.490 --> 00:18:04.810
Y-You think so?

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:08.940
But it doesn't hurt to be careful,
 so keep your guard up.

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:10.740
I know!

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:13.560
Huh?

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:15.820
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:18:16.060 --> 00:18:17.050
Yusha?!

00:18:19.250 --> 00:18:21.080
Hey, are you okay?!

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:23.920
I-I'm fine.

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:25.080
Huh?

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:26.980
Do these stairs...

00:18:29.060 --> 00:18:30.790
Search Cartado.

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:36.420
It would seem these stairs go 
all the way to the top floor.

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:38.290
Looks like there aren't any traps on them.

00:18:38.290 --> 00:18:39.840
Yay! Lucky us!

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:44.470
You really do have a Hero's 
talent for things like this.

00:18:51.050 --> 00:18:52.700
Oh, we're here!

00:18:52.700 --> 00:18:54.610
I'm pretty worn out.

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:56.240
Be careful!

00:18:56.350 --> 00:18:57.490
There's something here!

00:18:57.840 --> 00:19:00.410
So that's the boss of this tower, huh?

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:03.030
All right, everyone!

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:04.550
Let's go!

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:10.350
Huh?

00:19:10.350 --> 00:19:14.340
This guy's just a color variant of the 
monster we easily took out yesterday.

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:16.330
Oh, then this'll be easy!

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:17.460
Let's go!

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:18.400
Wait!

00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:20.960
Easy peasy!

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:22.930
Huh?! It's fast?!

00:19:24.920 --> 00:19:26.160
Watch out!

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:28.160
Even when monsters share the same form,

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:31.340
if their colors differ, their strength 
levels are completely different, too!

00:19:31.340 --> 00:19:33.120
I didn't know that.

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:34.260
I see...

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:36.960
Then let's be careful with it, everyone!

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:38.070
Yeah!

00:19:39.980 --> 00:19:41.620
Bam Bam Punch!

00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:43.200
Magic Arrow!

00:19:51.990 --> 00:19:53.340
Yes! We won!

00:19:53.340 --> 00:19:55.500
He was really strong.

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:57.130
I'm pooped.

00:19:57.130 --> 00:20:00.020
I even sank a rare Cartado on him.

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:04.740
It's Michael!

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:06.470
He's way up there?

00:20:08.490 --> 00:20:10.440
How do we rescue him?

00:20:13.720 --> 00:20:15.240
I can't reach him.

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:16.440
All right!

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:21.070
Nope...

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:24.200
I don't have any more Cartado I can use.

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:26.120
What do we do?

00:20:28.720 --> 00:20:29.830
I guess I must.

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:37.470
Right!

00:20:37.470 --> 00:20:39.660
A bow could cut through those threads!

00:20:39.660 --> 00:20:43.060
Huh? But I thought you weren't 
very good with a bow.

00:20:43.060 --> 00:20:44.090
That was a lie.

00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:47.870
The truth is I can't use a bow 
because my eyesight is bad.

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:50.910
I spent so much time reading books that I wound up nearsighted.

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:54.880
Hooray!

00:20:57.330 --> 00:20:59.220
Seira-chan, you're incredible!

00:20:59.220 --> 00:21:00.660
If you're that good,

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:03.660
why don't just wear glasses 
all the time and be an archer?

00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:05.310
Absolutely not!

00:21:05.310 --> 00:21:06.120
Why not?

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:09.950
Because people would think I'm a bookworm.

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:15.910
Hey! Why are you laughing?!

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:22.160
Here.

00:21:23.390 --> 00:21:24.740
Michael!

00:21:25.980 --> 00:21:27.220
I'm so glad!

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:29.850
Thank you, ladies!

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:31.600
You're welcome!

00:21:32.300 --> 00:21:33.470
Well, bye!

00:21:35.910 --> 00:21:37.640
Thank you!

00:21:41.260 --> 00:21:44.360
We went through a lot, 
but quests are fun, huh?

00:21:44.680 --> 00:21:45.610
Yeah!

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:47.550
They're not bad.

00:21:47.890 --> 00:21:49.540
Wait, no!

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:50.120
Huh?

00:21:50.520 --> 00:21:52.500
This wasn't a quest!

00:21:53.980 --> 00:21:55.750
The Silver Bone moss!

00:21:56.220 --> 00:21:58.640
We forgot about our real quest!

00:21:58.640 --> 00:21:59.800
This is bad!

00:21:59.800 --> 00:22:01.080
Oh, no!

00:22:01.080 --> 00:22:02.670
Let's hurry!

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
Ocean, Swimsuits, and Slaying Evil Gods!

00:23:35.920 --> 00:23:38.920
"Ocean, Swimsuits, and Slaying Evil Gods!"
